      "text": "This commit records v0.1.2 as published, but the release how-to still tells the reader to run `jj tag set v0.1.2` and `git push origin refs/tags/v0.1.2`, and its status text (lines 108-111) still names v0.1.1 as the latest stable release. The same section says never to reuse a released tag, so following the example now breaks that rule. Fix: change the example tag to a placeholder or the next unused version (for example `v0.1.3`), and add the v0.1.2 publication record next to the v0.1.1 record."
